# admino — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in all required values before running.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env
#
# NEVER commit .env to version control. It is listed in .gitignore.
# Secrets are passed to the container exclusively via environment variables —
# they are never baked into the image or written to the filesystem in plaintext.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM Provider
#
# This file (.env) is read ONLY by Docker Compose (env_file in docker-compose.yml).
# Local dev via `make run` does NOT load .env — it reads config/config.yaml plus
# your shell environment directly.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# LLM provider. config/config.yaml is the source of truth and defaults to
# "infomaniak" — Infomaniak AI Services, processed in Switzerland; queries are
# neither recorded nor used for training. Set INFOMANIAK_API_TOKEN below to chat.
# Without it admino still boots and chat replies explain what to set.
# Opt-ins: "vllm" runs a local model in a Docker CPU container (start it with
# `make start-local`, see the vLLM section below); "anthropic" and "openai" are
# cloud providers that send your messages to their servers — set the API key
# below and switch llm.provider in config.yaml (or via LLM_PROVIDER).
# LLM_PROVIDER is an override, left commented out so config.yaml's infomaniak wins.
# LLM_PROVIDER=infomaniak

# Infomaniak API token — REQUIRED for the default "infomaniak" provider.
# Create it in the Infomaniak Manager → API tokens (https://manager.infomaniak.com)
# with the `ai-tools` scope. Keep it secret: it is read from the environment
# only, never logged, and never sent to the browser.
INFOMANIAK_API_TOKEN=

# Infomaniak AI product ID — optional. When unset, admino discovers it at startup
# via GET https://api.infomaniak.com/1/ai. Set it when the token sees several AI
# products (startup then logs an error and chat asks for it); use the product_id
# of the product you want from that endpoint's response.
# INFOMANIAK_PRODUCT_ID=

# Anthropic API key — needed ONLY if you switch the provider to "anthropic".
# The default "infomaniak" provider does not use it, so this is opt-in: uncomment
# and fill it in to chat via Claude. Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OpenAI API key (required only when LLM_PROVIDER=openai).
# Get one at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional: point the openai provider at a self-hosted OpenAI-compatible server
# instead of the OpenAI cloud API. Defaults to https://api.openai.com/v1 when
# unset. OPENAI_API_KEY must still be set (any placeholder works for servers
# that don't check it), and in Docker mode the server's host must be allowed
# by the egress whitelist.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local vLLM serving (opt-in CPU container, cross-platform)
#
# vLLM is admino's optional local model, served by a Docker CPU container
# (vllm/vllm-openai-cpu:latest — multi-arch: Apple Silicon + Linux, no Metal,
# no host process). `make start` does NOT start it. Workflow:
#   make start-local    # provisions the ~8 GB model on first run, then brings
#                       # up postgres + agent + vllm
#   make vllm-pull      # (optional) pre-download / resume the model explicitly
# Then set llm.provider: "vllm" in config.yaml (or LLM_PROVIDER=vllm).
#
# The agent container reaches the vllm service at http://vllm:8000/v1 over the
# shared internal Docker bridge — no host aliases or extra egress rules needed.
#
# Trade-offs to be aware of:
#   - CPU inference is slow: expect a few tokens per second. A smaller model
#     (e.g. Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B-Instruct-2507) is snappier if throughput matters.
#   - Docker Desktop must have ~12–16 GB RAM allocated (Settings → Resources →
#     Memory). The default 8 GB is not enough for a 4B FP16 model.
#   - FP16 only (no 4-bit quant in the CPU image). Use the CUDA image for GPU.
#   - NVIDIA GPU serving: tracked in issue #132 (swap CPU image → CUDA image +
#     add a GPU reservation in docker-compose.yml).
#
# These variables override the matching config.yaml values. Leave them
# commented out to use the config.yaml defaults shown below.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# HuggingFace token — optional, only needed to download the vLLM model
# (`make start-local` / `make vllm-pull`) when the model repo is gated. Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 is public; set this only if you
# switch to a private/gated model. Never read at serve or runtime.
# HF_TOKEN=

# Model ID downloaded by `make start-local` / `make vllm-pull` and served by the
# vllm container.
# Default matches config.yaml: Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 (small, strong
# tool-caller; ~8 GB FP16). Override to any HuggingFace model the CPU image
# supports. For a snappier experience on slower hardware, try:
#   Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B-Instruct-2507  (~3 GB, faster but less capable)
# VLLM_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507

# OpenAI-compatible endpoint the agent uses to reach the vllm container.
# Points at the `vllm` Docker service over the internal bridge — do not change
# this unless you run vllm outside of docker-compose.
# VLLM_BASE_URL=http://vllm:8000/v1

# Maximum sequence length (tokens) the model will process.
# Raise this if you need longer context and have enough RAM; lower it to reduce
# KV-cache memory usage.
# VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192

# CPU KV-cache size in GB, pre-allocated on top of the model weights.
# Default 2 GB fits a 4B model in the ~16 GB Docker VM (weights ~7.5 GB + overhead
# leave ~3 GB free). If the engine dies at startup with "Available memory ... less
# than requested memory for kv", either lower this or give Docker Desktop more RAM.
# Raise it (e.g. 4) for more concurrency only after allocating ~20 GB+ to Docker.
# VLLM_CPU_KVCACHE_SPACE=2

# Tool-call parser vLLM uses to turn model output into OpenAI tool calls. Required
# for the agent's function calling (tool_choice="auto"). Must match the model's
# format: "hermes" for Qwen3/Qwen2.5 (default), "llama3_json" for Llama 3.x,
# "mistral" for Mistral. Wrong value => the model's tool calls won't be parsed.
# VLLM_TOOL_CALL_PARSER=hermes

# vLLM container image. Defaults to the multi-arch CPU image.
# To use NVIDIA GPU serving, swap this for the CUDA image (see issue #132).
# VLLM_IMAGE=vllm/vllm-openai-cpu:latest

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google OAuth (Gmail + Google Calendar + Google Drive)
# Required only if the gmail, google_calendar, or google_drive tools are
# enabled (permissions are managed in the database, seeded from
# admino.permissions.DEFAULT_PERMISSIONS on first run).
# Obtain credentials from https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Create an "OAuth 2.0 Client ID" of type "Desktop app".
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OAuth 2.0 Client ID from Google Cloud Console.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# OAuth 2.0 Client Secret from Google Cloud Console.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Microsoft OAuth (Outlook + Outlook Calendar + OneDrive)
# Required only if the outlook, outlook_calendar, or onedrive tools are
# enabled (permissions are managed in the database, seeded from
# admino.permissions.DEFAULT_PERMISSIONS on first run).
# Register an app at https://portal.azure.com/#view/Microsoft_AAD_RegisteredApps
# Use "Mobile and desktop applications" platform with redirect URI
# http://localhost:8000/oauth/callback.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Application (client) ID from Azure AD app registration.
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=

# Client secret from Azure AD app registration.
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Encryption
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Fernet symmetric encryption key used to encrypt OAuth refresh tokens at rest.
# The ciphertext is stored in PostgreSQL (oauth_tokens table); this key stays
# in the environment only and is never written to the database.
# Generate a new key with:
#   python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
# IMPORTANT: Keep this key secret. Losing it makes stored tokens unrecoverable.
# IMPORTANT: Rotating this key requires re-running the OAuth consent flow.
# The code reads this as OAUTH_ENCRYPTION_KEY.
OAUTH_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# admino uses two database roles (see docs/SECURITY.md → Database roles):
#   - the owner `admino` (a superuser) owns the schema and runs the migrations,
#     in the one-shot `migrate` service (or `make migrate`), and nothing else;
#   - the runtime role `admino_app` (not a superuser) is what the app connects
#     as. It can't change the schema or rewrite the audit log.

# Password of the owner role `admino`. Change it before the first run: Postgres
# sets it when it creates the data volume, and on an existing volume it must stay
# the password the volume was created with. Never given to the running app.
# Generate with: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# May contain any characters — admino URL-encodes it before connecting.
PG_PASSWORD=changeme

# Password of the runtime role `admino_app`. REQUIRED, also when upgrading an
# existing install: the migrate step stops without it. Printable ASCII only, and
# it must differ from PG_PASSWORD. The migrate step sets it on every start, so
# changing it here and restarting rotates it.
# Generate with: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
PG_APP_PASSWORD=changeme-app

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transactional email (SMTP)
#
# One SMTP account for the whole platform: invitations, password resets and
# account/budget/model/deletion notices for every organization go out through
# it. We recommend a Swiss-based provider, e.g. Infomaniak Mail:
#   SMTP_HOST=mail.infomaniak.com, SMTP_PORT=587 (or 465), the full mailbox
#   address as SMTP_USERNAME, and that address (or one of its aliases) as
#   SMTP_FROM — providers usually reject other senders.
#
# TLS is required: 587 = STARTTLS, 465 = implicit TLS, with certificate
# verification. Other ports (e.g. 25) are refused.
# In Docker, entrypoint.sh opens egress to exactly SMTP_HOST:SMTP_PORT.
# Leave all five unset to run without email: admino still starts, logs which
# variables are missing, and keeps messages queued until SMTP is configured.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SMTP server hostname (a dotted hostname, not an IP address).
# SMTP_HOST=mail.infomaniak.com

# 587 (STARTTLS) or 465 (implicit TLS).
# SMTP_PORT=587

# SMTP login, usually the full mailbox address.
# SMTP_USERNAME=

# SMTP password. Keep it secret: read from the environment only, never logged.
# SMTP_PASSWORD=

# Sender address (the From header), e.g. noreply@your-domain.ch.
# SMTP_FROM=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paths (container-internal)
# These defaults match the volume mounts in docker-compose.yml.
# Only change if you customise the volume layout.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Directory where config.yaml is mounted (read-only).
CONFIG_DIR=/app/config

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Set to "production" for production deployments. In production mode:
#   - Stricter validation on startup
# Leave unset or "development" for local dev.
ADMINO_ENV=production

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server / Logging
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Log level for the Python application logger.
# One of: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR, CRITICAL
LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Log line format: text (default) or json (one JSON object per line with ts,
# level, logger, message and request_id, for a log collector). Logs hold IDs,
# counts and statuses only, never content, tracebacks or URL query strings.
LOG_FORMAT=text

# Session cookie Secure flag (default: true). Keep it on: the login cookie is
# then only sent over HTTPS, and Chrome and Firefox also accept Secure cookies
# on http://localhost, so local use works as is. false is a development-only
# setting: use it ONLY when you open a laptop install over plain HTTP from
# another address (e.g. a phone on your LAN reaching http://192.168.x.y:8000),
# otherwise the browser drops the cookie and login never sticks. admino refuses
# to start with false when ADMINO_PUBLIC_URL is https, and the production
# profile always sets true.
# COOKIE_SECURE=false

# The address users open admino at: an origin like https://admino.example.ch,
# without a path (default: http://localhost:8000). Password reset and
# invitation links are built from it, never from the request's Host header,
# and it's the only origin CORS allows. It must be https; plain http is only
# allowed for localhost, 127.0.0.1 and [::1]. Production deployments MUST set
# it, otherwise emailed links point at localhost (the production profile sets
# it to https://ADMINO_DOMAIN). An invalid value stops admino at startup.
# ADMINO_PUBLIC_URL=https://admino.example.ch

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production profile (docker-compose.prod.yml, `make start-prod`)
#
# A Caddy reverse proxy terminates TLS with an automatic Let's Encrypt
# certificate, redirects HTTP to HTTPS and sends HSTS. The agent publishes no
# port. Point the domain's DNS A record at the server and open ports 80 and 443
# inbound before the first start. The laptop targets (`make start`) ignore these.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The public hostname, without scheme or path. The production profile serves
# https://ADMINO_DOMAIN and sets ADMINO_PUBLIC_URL, COOKIE_SECURE=true and
# ADMINO_TRUSTED_PROXIES for the agent (overriding the values in this file).
# Use localhost to try the profile on a laptop with Caddy's local certificate
# authority instead of Let's Encrypt.
# ADMINO_DOMAIN=admino.example.ch

# The reverse proxies whose X-Forwarded-For / X-Forwarded-Proto headers admino
# believes: comma-separated IP addresses or CIDR ranges (default: none). The
# client IP from X-Forwarded-For feeds per-IP rate limits and audit events, so
# list only your own proxy. The production profile sets Caddy's fixed address
# (172.31.0.10/32); set it yourself only for another proxy in front of admino.
# A range covering every address (0.0.0.0/0, ::/0) and invalid entries stop
# admino at startup.
# ADMINO_TRUSTED_PROXIES=172.31.0.10/32

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Egress whitelist (iptables)
# The whitelist of hostnames the agent may reach on port 443 lives in
# config/config.yaml under egress.allowed_hosts — the single source of truth.
# entrypoint.sh derives the iptables rules from it at container startup;
# there is no env var to keep in sync. The default provider's host
# (api.infomaniak.com) and api.anthropic.com are whitelisted out of the box.
# Switching to OpenAI? Uncomment api.openai.com in config.yaml.
#
# REQUIRE_EGRESS_WHITELIST: hard-fail startup if the iptables whitelist cannot
# be applied. Keep "true" for production safety — the agent container has the
# NET_ADMIN capability (see docker-compose.yml) and the entrypoint applies the
# rules as root, then drops to the unprivileged admino user, so enforcement
# works out of the box. Set to "false" ONLY for local runs without Docker
# privileges: the whitelist is then skipped with a warning (never in production).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REQUIRE_EGRESS_WHITELIST=true
